Package: t2-utils
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: zhongfu <me@zhongfu.li>
Depends: python3, python3-dbus, python3-gi, bluez, cloud-guest-utils, dnsmasq, e2fsprogs, iproute2, libubootenv-tool, network-manager, openssh-client, systemd
Recommends: iw
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Description: ZSpace T2 board support files
 The board userspace for the ZSpace T2 (Rockchip RK3568) image: the systemd
 units and their enablement, the /etc drop-ins (NetworkManager, dnsmasq,
 sshd, logind, systemd, power-button policy), the /usr/local/sbin helper
 scripts, and t2-mkfit, which assembles the boot FIT (kernel + device tree +
 initramfs) the board's U-Boot reads.
 .
 The files under /etc are conffiles, so local edits survive an upgrade.  The
 same .deb ships in a local apt repository inside the image (/opt/t2/repo),
 so a board can reinstall or upgrade the package offline, without reflashing.
